From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tcdent <tcdent@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 16:24:58 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 36/38] fs: sharedfs: reclaim window space for page faults

A fault that finds the window full cannot reclaim, as it holds its
file's invalidate lock, so it backs off with EAGAIN and retries. Nothing
guaranteed that anyone reclaimed meanwhile; a workload that only mmaps
would retry forever. Such a fault now queues a reclaim work item, which
holds no locks and frees a batch of idle chunks.

Request completion and notification delivery become separate work
items. Completion takes only the queue lock, so a request made while
holding the mount lock (reclaim) or from inside notification delivery
(an inode's last reference dropped by an event) is always answered;
with one work item for both, it waited on itself.

Chunk mapping failures other than EAGAIN are now logged: on a fault
they become SIGBUS, and they left no trace.

Reported-by: tablet.lead@a10k.internal
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SKmspe5nVbuvzdvYZa9UhW
---
